  "seconds": 120.1,
  "rules": "A group \"moves\" in a frame when its world matrix changed since the last audited frame (by more than 1e-6). Groups that moved by the same rigid motion (a MiR with its cabinet, its holders and the parts on them) form one cluster and are not checked against each other: their relative poses didn't change, so no new contact can appear between them. Every visible body of a moving group is checked against every other visible body except its own group's subtree and ancestors, the arms and what they hold (the arm checks do those), and liquids: world boxes first, all at once, then FCL on the meshes of the pairs whose boxes overlap (BVHs built only for those). The contacts a group had at its last pose before it started moving are its baseline and are left out while it keeps moving, until that pair comes apart; a new contact counts if depth() puts it deeper than DEPTH_MM (1.5 mm), so a tray set down on a table or a MiR rolling onto a floor plate isn't reported."
 },
